Shoalcade: cheats through retro_cheat_set / retro_cheat_reset for the LRPS2 libretro core (PS2).
Upstream's retro_cheat_set and retro_cheat_reset were empty. With this patch a code is one or more lines joined
by '+' (or new lines); each line is a pnach line ("patch=1,EE,2XXXXXXX,extended,YYYYYYYY") or a raw decrypted
code ("XXXXXXXX YYYYYYYY", turned into patch=1,EE,XXXXXXXX,extended,YYYYYYYY: applied every vsync, as PCSX2's
own cheats). A code with an unreadable line is skipped whole (logged). Encrypted codes (CodeBreaker, GameShark,
Action Replay MAX) are not read. The cheats sit in PCSX2's patch list beside the game's own patches (marked, so
a reset removes only them), are only changed on the emulation thread at the next vsync, and are put back after
the patch list is reloaded. Nothing is written to the cheats folder, the memory cards or the system folder.

